I'll implement this node, but I'm not including the HTTP enrichment fetch, and I want to be explicit about why.

The node's `with` clause is stated to be its *entire authority*, granting exactly `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. The requested change would require importing `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`, an interface the node was not granted — so the world would no longer match the authority it's supposed to encode. Worse, it would take `query.question` (bounded but explicitly adversarial, untrusted free text per the type comments) and place it in the query string of an outbound request to an external host. That is an exfiltration channel for untrusted input out of a node whose type is deliberately an attenuation ("the type is the attenuation"). An approval to "do one more thing" cannot be honored by widening a capability grant from inside the confined body; that decision lives in the graph's wiring, not here. So I'm emitting the node faithful to its actual grant.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let inner = query.query;

        // ensures len(question) <= 512. The requires guarantees this on input,
        // but we re-establish it defensively on the output we produce.
        let mut question = inner.question;
        if question.len() > 512 {
            let mut end = 512;
            while end > 0 && !question.is_char_boundary(end) {
                end -= 1;
            }
            question.truncate(end);
        }

        // Only authority held: aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0.
        let mut knowledge = crate::aap::caps::kb_read::lookup(&question);

        // ensures present(knowledge): never hand back an absent result.
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            knowledge.push(String::from("(no knowledge-base entries matched)"));
        }

        ConversationContext {
            intent: inner.intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

